Apple's next product announcement is already approaching, with the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/19/apple-october-28-product-launch/">"Pro and tell" experience</a> scheduled for October 28 in Los Angeles. Redesigned 14-inch and 16-inch MacBook Pro models are expected to headline the announcements, combining OLED displays with the first touchscreens on a Mac.<br/>
<br/>
The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/touchscreen-macbook-pro/">redesigned machines</a> are rumored to feature lighter, potentially thinner designs, a reinforced hinge for touch input, and a Dynamic Island replacing the "notch." They are expected to retain M5 Pro and M5 Max chips, making the display and design the main new features. <br/>
<br/>
A <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/20/ipad-mini-8-10-rumored-features/">redesigned iPad mini</a> is also expected, featuring an OLED display, the A20 Pro chip, a landscape front-facing camera, and a redesigned speaker system. Water resistance could also be present for the first time on an iPad. Apple is also expected to bring the M6 chip to the iMac and entry-level 14-inch MacBook Pro.<br/>
<br/>
